sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: a synchronous read of the Metrics role through Grafana; no run, no stored sample. docs/reference/metrics.md#read-node-metrics.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: node:metrics
  %% kind: node.metrics
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane M icon=server pill=observer tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant M as Metrics<br/>Grafana · Prom.
  CLI->>GW: node:metrics NODE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:metrics NODE`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> [--json]`
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate the Node
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has an access grant to the target Node
  %%> - the target is active and has a WireGuard address (`node.metrics_unavailable`)
  %%> - exactly one active Node holds the Metrics role and has stored credentials (`metrics.assignment_missing`, `metrics.assignment_drift`, `metrics.node_inactive`, `metrics.credentials_missing`)
  %%> Why no run:
  %%> - the command only reads; it starts no run, changes no Node and stores no sample
  GW->>M: Read the exporter<br/>memory · swap · load · uptime
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one query for memory, swap, load and uptime; it alone decides whether the Node has metrics
  GW->>M: Read cores, pressure<br/>and disks · three queries
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one query each; pseudo filesystems such as `tmpfs` and `proc` are left out, and `/` comes first
  %%> - if one of them fails, its field is empty (pressure `0`) and the command still succeeds
  alt Prometheus answered
    M-->>GW: samples
    GW-->>CLI: 200 OK<br/>one snapshot
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the snapshot with the Node's name and ID; pressure is `0` when the kernel has no pressure data
  else Grafana did not answer, or no samples yet
    M--xGW: no answer or no samples
    GW--xCLI: 502 Bad Gateway<br/>node.metrics_unreachable
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing is stored or changed; run the command again once the Node's exporter has reported
  end
